tools.description:
Append an event to a DPP. Recalling a unit is an event here: a status change to suspended, so the passport goes on answering a scan with the recall.
Permission: dpp_events. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: append_dpp_event {"event":{"eventType":"inspection","description":"Annual safety inspection passed","publish":true,"data":{"workshopId":"DE-4711"}},"id":"<id>"}

Create DPPs in bulk. Rows are deduplicated by their identifiers, so resubmitting after a timeout creates nothing twice.
Permission: dpp_bulk_write. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: bulk_create_dpps {"rows":[{"modelIdentifier":"FC-50ML"}]}

Validate DPPs in bulk
Permission: dpp_bulk_write. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: bulk_validate_dpps {"rows":[{"modelIdentifier":"FC-50ML"}]}

Create a brand
Permission: one of brand_access, brand_write. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: create_brand {"brand":{"name":"Natura Care"}}

Create a component
Permission: one of component_access, component_write. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: create_component {"component":{"name":"Shea Butter"},"properties":{"new":{"12":[{"value":"Emollient"}]}},"templateIds":["507"]}

Create a DPP
Permission: dpp_write. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: create_dpp {"dpp":{"unlockableType":"Product","unlockableId":11,"description":"Hydrating Face Cream 50ml","granularity":"item","batchIdentifier":"L2026-09","serialIdentifier":"000412","propertyTypeIds":[]}}

Upload a mediafile. A link goes in under url and the server reads the bytes; a small image can go in as base64 under data.
Permission: none beyond a valid token. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: create_mediafile {"mediafile":{"url":"https://images.example.com/rain-shell-hero.jpg","name":"Rain shell hero shot"}}

Create a product. Call product_property_types first: a product missing a mandatory property is refused.
Permission: product_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: create_product {"brand":{"name":"NaturaCare"},"product":{"name":"Hydrating Face Cream","gtin":"4006381333931","componentsInput":["Aqua","Glycerin","Cetearyl Alcohol"]}}

Create a webhook subscription. The answer carries the signing secret, shown only here.
Permission: webhook_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: create_webhook {"webhook":{"url":"https://hooks.example.com/transpareo","eventTypes":["published","voided"]}}

Delete a webhook subscription
Permission: webhook_access. Cannot be undone; confirm must be "delete <id>". Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: delete_webhook {"confirm":"delete <id>","id":"<id>"}

What a passport of a product needs. The answer carries a body ready to fill for validate_dpp and create_dpp.
Permission: dpp_read. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: dpp_requirements {"productId":"<productId>"}

Get a component
Permission: none, the endpoint is public. Data tier: public.
Example: get_component {"id":"<id>"}

Read a DPP
Permission: dpp_read. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: get_dpp {"id":"<id>"}

Get a lot
Permission: dpp_read. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: get_lot {"id":"<id>"}

Get a product
Permission: none, the endpoint is public. Data tier: public.
Example: get_product {"id":"<id>"}

List brands
Permission: none, the endpoint is public. Data tier: public.
Example: list_brands {"per_page":20}

List components
Permission: none, the endpoint is public. Data tier: public.
Example: list_components {"per_page":20}

List Digital Product Passports
Permission: dpp_read. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: list_dpps {"per_page":20}

List exports
Permission: export_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: list_exports {"per_page":20}

List imports. The runs this credential started, newest first. A run begun earlier, or in another session, is found again here.
Permission: import_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: list_imports {"per_page":20}

List lots. The lots batch and item passports freeze from. Narrow by product_id or identifier; a lot is created by the first passport that names it, never here.
Permission: dpp_read. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: list_lots {"per_page":20}

List mediafiles
Permission: none beyond a valid token. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: list_mediafiles {"per_page":20}

List products
Permission: none, the endpoint is public. Data tier: public.
Example: list_products {"per_page":20}

List webhook subscriptions
Permission: webhook_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: list_webhooks {"per_page":20}

What the presented token allows. Start here: what the credential allows, its scope and rate limit.
Permission: none beyond a valid token. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: me {}

Get new product template. The property types a new product can carry, with the mandatory ones flagged: the body create_product needs.
Permission: none, the endpoint is public. Data tier: public.
Example: product_property_types {}

Publish a DPP. Signs a snapshot into the ten-year archive. Publishing cannot be undone.
Permission: dpp_write. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: publish_dpp {"code":"<code>","reason":"edit"}

Publish a product. A storefront action: a workspace without one publishes a product as it is created and answers 403 here.
Permission: product_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: publish_product {"id":"<id>"}

Read a help article. One article whole, as markdown, with the address of the page a person opens it at.
Permission: none beyond a valid token. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: read_help {"key":"<key>"}

Rotate a webhook secret. The old secret stops working at once; the answer carries the new one, shown only here.
Permission: webhook_access. Cannot be undone; confirm must be "regenerate <id>". Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: regenerate_webhook_secret {"confirm":"regenerate <id>","id":"<id>"}

Reissue a DPP
Permission: dpp_lifecycle. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: reissue_dpp {"description":"QR label reprinted after damage","id":"<id>","successorCode":"F9G8H7J6K"}

Search the help articles. How a person does something in the application manager, from the articles it shows them. Give term the question in the reader's own words. A call with no term answers the whole set, which is how an empty answer is told apart from a workspace whose help content has not arrived.
Permission: none beyond a valid token. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: search_help {"per_page":20}

Supersede a DPP
Permission: dpp_lifecycle. Cannot be undone; confirm must be "supersede <id>". Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: supersede_dpp {"confirm":"supersede <id>","description":"Replaced under warranty","id":"<id>","successorCode":"F9G8H7J6K"}

Send a test delivery
Permission: webhook_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: test_webhook {"id":"<id>"}

Unpublish a product
Permission: product_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: unpublish_product {"id":"<id>"}

Update a component
Permission: one of component_access, component_write. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: update_component {"component":{"name":"Shea Butter"},"id":"<id>","properties":{"new":{"12":[{"value":"Emollient"}]},"existing":{"14":{"811":{"value":"ES"}}}},"templateIds":["507"]}

Update a DPP
Permission: dpp_write. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: update_dpp {"dpp":{"description":"Updated description"},"id":"<id>"}

Update dynamic data
Permission: dpp_dynamic. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: update_dynamic_data {"dynamicData":{"stateOfHealth":87.3,"cycleCount":412,"retiredReason":null},"id":"<id>"}

Update a product
Permission: product_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: update_product {"id":"<id>","product":{"name":"Updated Product Name"}}

Update product mediafile assignments. Replaces a product's images with the ones named, in the order given.
Permission: product_access. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: update_product_mediafiles {"id":"<id>","mediafileIds":[24,25]}

Validate a DPP payload. Runs the checks a publish runs, writes nothing. Call it before create_dpp.
Permission: dpp_write. Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: validate_dpp {"dpp":{"unlockableType":"Product","unlockableId":11,"granularity":"item","batchIdentifier":"L2026-09","serialIdentifier":"000412"}}

Void a DPP. For a unit that no longer exists. To recall one that is still in the field, use append_dpp_event instead.
Permission: dpp_lifecycle. Cannot be undone; confirm must be "void <id>". Data tier: authorised (the workspace's own catalogue).
Example: void_dpp {"confirm":"void <id>","description":"Unit scrapped in final inspection, never left the plant","id":"<id>","reason":"never_shipped"}
